op, checking is the optimal strategy. It avoids bloating the pot while I am behind and gives me a chance to see the turn card for free to complete my flush.\nAnswer: 0\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: You hold a Flush Draw with the 8 of Diamonds and the three diamonds on the board (Qd, 4d, 2d). You have 9 outs to complete the flush, which is a strong drawing hand. However, your current hand is only 8-high, which has no showdown value. The pot is small as it was limped pre-flop. Acting first, betting is risky as it opens you up to a raise which would make seeing the next card expensive. Checking allows you to potentially see the Turn card for free to hit your flush.\n\nReason: You have a strong flush draw but currently only high-card value. Checking is the safest play to try to hit your flush without inflating the pot prematurely.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
